---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Support & SLA — Isogun Labs"
  description="Support hours and response-time commitment for Isogun Labs apps, including Recap, Field Hygiene for Jira, and Passdown."
  path="/support/"
  ogDescription="Support hours and response-time commitment for Isogun Labs apps."
>

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="kicker">Support</div>
    <h1>Support &amp; <span class="amber">SLA</span></h1>
    <p>Isogun Labs is an independent studio, not a large vendor with a dedicated support team — this page states plainly what to expect. It applies across every Isogun Labs app: Recap, Field Hygiene for Jira, Passdown, and any future release.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="block reveal">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px;">

    <h2>How to reach us</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:support@isogunlabs.com">support@isogunlabs.com</a> for any question,
      bug report, or issue with an Isogun Labs app. This is the same address used for security
      reports and general product questions — one inbox, read directly by the team building the
      apps.
    </p>

    <h2>Hours of operation</h2>
    <div class="week-strip" role="img" aria-label="Available Monday through Friday, closed Saturday and Sunday">
      <span class="day off">S</span>
      <span class="day on">M</span>
      <span class="day on">T</span>
      <span class="day on">W</span>
      <span class="day on">T</span>
      <span class="day on">F</span>
      <span class="day off">S</span>
    </div>
    <p>
      Support is available <strong class="amber">Monday through Friday</strong>, during standard
      business hours. We do not currently offer weekend or holiday coverage.
    </p>

    <h2>Response-time commitment</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to respond to every support request within <strong>one business day</strong> of
      receipt. This is a response-time commitment, not a resolution-time guarantee — some issues
      take longer to fully resolve, but you will hear back from us within one business day
      acknowledging the request and outlining next steps.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This commitment covers Isogun Labs' own apps specifically. It does not cover the underlying
      availability of Atlassian Jira or Atlassian Forge itself, which is governed by Atlassian's
      own platform SLAs — Isogun Labs apps run entirely on Forge and have no separate
      infrastructure of their own to offer an independent uptime guarantee for.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:32px;">Product-specific security and privacy details live on each app's own site &mdash; see <a href="https://field-hygiene.isogunlabs.com/security.html">Field&nbsp;Hygiene's&nbsp;Security&nbsp;Policy</a> or <a href="https://recap.isogunlabs.com/">Recap</a> for the app you're evaluating.</p>

  </div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .week-strip { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin: 18px 0 14px; }
  .week-strip .day {
    width: 42px;
    height: 42px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: .82rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .02em;
  }
  .week-strip .day.on {
    background: var(--black);
    color: var(--white);
  }
  .week-strip .day.off {
    background: var(--panel);
    color: var(--body);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .week-strip .day { width: 36px; height: 36px; font-size: .76rem; }
  }
</style>
